sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as External Client
    participant Route as OpenShift Route<br/>443/TCP HTTPS TLS 1.2+
    participant KRBP as kube-rbac-proxy<br/>8443/TCP HTTPS
    participant TAS as TrustyAI Service<br/>8080/TCP HTTP
    participant InfSvc as KServe InferenceService<br/>varies HTTPS

    Note over Client,InfSvc: Flow 1: TrustyAI Service → InferenceService Payload Capture

    Client->>Route: POST /v1/info<br/>HTTPS/443 TLS 1.2+
    Route->>KRBP: Forward (edge TLS)<br/>HTTPS/8443
    KRBP->>KRBP: SubjectAccessReview<br/>Bearer Token
    KRBP->>TAS: Proxy to localhost<br/>HTTP/8080 (no TLS)
    TAS->>InfSvc: Patch Logger URL<br/>HTTPS (serving cert)
    InfSvc-->>TAS: Payload Data
    TAS-->>KRBP: Response
    KRBP-->>Route: Response
    Route-->>Client: JSON Response

    participant User as User / kubectl
    participant K8sAPI as Kubernetes API<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant LMESCtrl as LMES Controller
    participant EvalPod as LMEval Pod
    participant Driver as ta-lmes-driver<br/>18080/TCP HTTP
    participant HF as HuggingFace Hub<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant OCI as OCI Registry<br/>443/TCP HTTPS

    Note over User,OCI: Flow 2: LMEvalJob Execution

    User->>K8sAPI: Create LMEvalJob CR<br/>HTTPS/443 TLS 1.2+<br/>RBAC: lmeval-user-role
    K8sAPI->>LMESCtrl: Watch event
    LMESCtrl->>K8sAPI: Create Pod<br/>ServiceAccount token
    Note over EvalPod,Driver: Init container copies driver binary<br/>to shared emptyDir volume
    EvalPod->>HF: Download model/datasets<br/>HTTPS/443 TLS 1.2+
    EvalPod->>Driver: Status updates<br/>HTTP/18080 (localhost)
    LMESCtrl->>EvalPod: Pod exec (SPDY)<br/>ServiceAccount
    Driver->>OCI: Upload results (optional)<br/>HTTPS/443 TLS 1.2+<br/>Auth: dockerConfigJson

    participant EHRoute as OpenShift Route<br/>443/TCP passthrough
    participant EHKRBP as kube-rbac-proxy<br/>8443/TCP HTTPS
    participant EvalHub as EvalHub API<br/>8444/TCP HTTP
    participant PG as PostgreSQL<br/>5432/TCP
    participant OTLP as OTLP Collector

    Note over Client,OTLP: Flow 3: EvalHub Multi-Tenant API

    Client->>EHRoute: API Request<br/>HTTPS/443 TLS 1.2+ (passthrough)
    EHRoute->>EHKRBP: Forward<br/>HTTPS/8443 (serving cert)
    EHKRBP->>EHKRBP: SubjectAccessReview<br/>Bearer Token
    EHKRBP->>EvalHub: Proxy to localhost<br/>HTTP/8444
    EvalHub->>PG: Query/Store data<br/>PostgreSQL/5432 TLS (optional)<br/>Auth: username/password
    EvalHub->>OTLP: Telemetry export<br/>gRPC/HTTP TLS (optional)
    EvalHub-->>EHKRBP: Response
    EHKRBP-->>EHRoute: Response
    EHRoute-->>Client: JSON Response

    participant GRoute as OpenShift Route<br/>443/TCP reencrypt
    participant GKRBP as kube-rbac-proxy<br/>8432/TCP HTTPS
    participant Orch as Orchestrator<br/>8032/TCP HTTPS
    participant Detector as Detector InferenceService<br/>HTTPS
    participant GenSvc as Generation InferenceService<br/>HTTPS
    participant BuiltIn as Built-in Detector<br/>8080/TCP HTTP

    Note over Client,BuiltIn: Flow 4: Guardrails Orchestrator Pipeline

    Client->>GRoute: POST /api/v1/chat<br/>HTTPS/443 TLS 1.2+ (reencrypt)
    GRoute->>GKRBP: Forward<br/>HTTPS/8432 TLS
    GKRBP->>GKRBP: SubjectAccessReview<br/>Bearer Token (if auth enabled)
    GKRBP->>Orch: Proxy<br/>HTTPS/8032 (serving cert)
    Orch->>Detector: Detection request<br/>HTTPS (serving cert)
    Detector-->>Orch: Detection result
    Orch->>BuiltIn: Regex detection<br/>HTTP/8080 (localhost)
    BuiltIn-->>Orch: Detection result
    Orch->>GenSvc: Generation request<br/>HTTPS (serving cert)
    GenSvc-->>Orch: Generated response
    Orch-->>GKRBP: Guarded response
    GKRBP-->>GRoute: Response
    GRoute-->>Client: JSON Response
